    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "QA report signing — two routes, chosen by the performer's reach",
      "prov:value": "`folio-test-run/v1` (`schemas/sdlc/test-run.ts`)\nanswers the first: a data hash and a process hash, each all-or-nothing, plus\nthe `skill` it tests, whose contract its recorded `cases` are checked against\n(`test-run-conforms`, #1168).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1168"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "QA report signing — two routes, chosen by the performer's reach",
      "prov:value": "From the owner, 2026-09-20 on\n[#363](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/363):\n\n> some of the machine actors may be air-gapped, it is a property of an actor.\n> depending on the propeorty, different tools might not work. in this case an\n> API wouldnt wokr and a human actor is needed. so process for signing needs\n> two parallel routes/processes, air gapped vs not, the first needed a human\n> actor",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#363",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "QA report signing — two routes, chosen by the performer's reach",
      "prov:value": "The subject is the **QA report** — owner, same day, answering what gets\nsigned."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "QA report signing — two routes, chosen by the performer's reach",
      "prov:value": "**This skill builds on [`signing`](signing.md)** (owner, option B,\n2026-10-30).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Reach is a property of the ACTOR, and `unknown` is a third state",
      "prov:value": "**One vocabulary, two levels.** An actor's `reach` uses the same scale as\n   the deployment's `network` (`folio-assistant-g7vb`) — `internet`,\n   `egress-restricted`, `air-gapped`."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why there is no `network-egress` capability",
      "prov:value": "The bean (`folio-assistant-r0rq`) proposed one, reasoning that\n`CapabilityDefinition.requires` already propagates dependencies and an\nair-gapped actor would simply not carry it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why there is no `network-egress` capability",
      "prov:value": "Worse, the capability\nwould have carried the same fact as `reach`, in a second place, free to\ndisagree — bean `ind9` is the fixed instance of putting non-probeable things\nin `capabilities[]`, and this would have reopened it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ind9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaration and execution are different mechanisms",
      "prov:value": "`fallbackRole` (bean `folio-assistant-85e8`) says **which lane takes over**\nwhen no capability can do it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-85e8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaration and execution are different mechanisms",
      "prov:value": "Re-measured 2026-09-20 —\n**nothing invokes that script**, it is in no `package.json` entry and no\nworkflow, and its output directory `schemas/generated/` does not exist.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "proposal",
      "cat-harness:section": "Declaration and execution are different mechanisms",
      "prov:value": "(`folio-assistant-3lbz`, and\n`cat-harness/docs/proposals/zod-schemas-as-tools.md`.)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "docs/proposals/zod-schemas-as-tools.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the signed report goes: the `qa-reports` branch, next to its run",
      "prov:value": "A QA report is a **derived** record — it can be rebuilt from the tree and the\ndata it hashed — so since arc `3fva` it is kept where every derived QA result\nis kept: the orphan **`qa-reports`** branch, in the entry keyed by the commit\nit judged (`main/<sha>/` or `pr/<n>/<sha>/`), written through\n`scripts/qa-store.ts` and never by a hand `git push`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3fva"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/qa-report-signing.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the signed report goes: the `qa-reports` branch, next to its run",
      "prov:value": "**What does not go there.** A **certification** — an accountable role's\nDecision taken on a test report's rollup — is a separate node, and it stays\non `main` beside the attestations (owner decision D5, default (a)): it is a\njudgement, the same class as `test/attestations/`, and no regeneration can\nreproduce it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "D5"
      ]
    }
  ]
